# Diagrams must be Mermaid

In this repo (docs, README, comments, and user-facing text), every diagram is a fenced `mermaid` block. Do not use ASCII boxes, arrows (`──►`, `└──`), PlantUML, Graphviz, or screenshots of topology.

Follow Mermaid syntax that MkDocs can render:

- No spaces in node IDs. Use camelCase or quotes on labels: `kafka[Kafka cluster telemetry]`
- Quote edge labels that contain parentheses, slashes, or colons
- Subgraphs need an ID and a label: `subgraph hosts [RHEL]`
- Do not use `end` as a node ID

```text
# BAD
RHEL rsyslog ──► ArcSight
            └──► omkafka ──► rhel-system-logs

# GOOD
flowchart TB
  rsyslog[rsyslog]
  arcsight[ArcSight]
  logs[rhel-system-logs]
  rsyslog -->|"omfwd or omrelp"| arcsight
  rsyslog -->|omkafka| logs
```
